---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const stages = [
  { n: '01', name: 'Interrogate', body: 'Short, specific questions come before any advice, scaled to the stakes: a small reversible call gets three sharp questions, a one-way-door call gets up to six.' },
  { n: '02', name: 'Challenge the framing', body: 'The stated decision is tested once against the real one, so a solution chosen before the thinking was done gets caught rather than built around.' },
  { n: '03', name: 'Play it back', body: 'Your situation is reflected back in a few lines, and any tension in what you have said (a fixed deadline against an unapproved budget, a stated risk appetite against the option you favour) is named for you to resolve.' },
  { n: '04', name: 'Reason', body: 'Options are generated, including the ones you did not bring and doing nothing. Constraints you have treated as fixed are tested against what you have actually verified.' },
  { n: '05', name: 'Produce', body: 'The five-part Decision Brief, written in clean markdown, with a self-check before it is handed to you.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="The Decision · GreenSquare"
  description="The Decision is a single file that turns Claude or GPT into a decision advisor. It interrogates before it answers, then produces a five-part, evidence-tagged brief."
  current="product"
>
  <section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="container grid-split">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="overline">The product</p>
        <h1 class="h1">The Decision.</h1>
        <p class="lead mt-6">
          One file that interrogates before it answers: it questions you, tests the framing once, plays your
          situation back to you and catches contradictions, then produces genuine options and an evidence-tagged
          recommendation with a self-check, all in markdown. Twelve months of model-version updates included.
        </p>
        <div class="action-row">
          <a class="btn btn-on-dark" href="https://buy.stripe.com/aFaaEWfGDc7W7XF2wv3AY00" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get the Decision, $49</a>
          <a class="text-action" href="/benchmark/">See the benchmark</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal reveal-d1">
        <div class="specimen-card panel-on-dark">
          <p class="mono specimen-tag">01–05</p>
          <ol class="specimen-list-simple">
            {stages.map((s) => <li>{s.name}</li>)}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="overline">What it is</p>
      <h2 class="maxw-30ch">A disciplined thinking partner for one decision, not another chat window.</h2>
      <p class="measure mt-6">
        The Decision turns a generic AI account into a decision advisor for a single real call. Open a new chat,
        paste or upload the file, and describe the decision you are facing in your own words. It leads from
        there: it asks before it advises, tests whether the decision you named is the real one, and only then
        builds the brief. It behaves the same way on Claude and GPT, because the discipline is written into the
        file, not left to the model's mood on the day.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-paper">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="overline">The method</p>
      <h2>Five stages, in order, every time.</h2>
      <p class="measure mt-4">It does not skip to the brief. Each stage exists because the one before it changes what the brief should say.</p>
      <div class="stage-grid">
        {stages.map((s) => (
          <article class="reveal">
            <span class="mono stage-num">{s.n}</span>
            <h3>{s.name}</h3>
            <p class="small mt-2">{s.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="overline">The output</p>
      <h2>Five parts, every time.</h2>
      <div class="output-grid">
        <div class="card"><span class="mono">1</span><h3>The decision, and why now</h3><p class="small">The real decision, and what makes it live today.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="mono">2</span><h3>The options, compared</h3><p class="small">A compact table, scored against the criteria that matter, including the options you did not bring.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="mono">3</span><h3>The recommendation</h3><p class="small">The call, and the one or two assumptions it rests on, each tagged given, inferred or unknown.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="mono">4</span><h3>Next steps</h3><p class="small">Three to five concrete actions, sequenced if the clock matters.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="mono">5</span><h3>What would change this call</h3><p class="small">The specific risks or unknowns that would flip the recommendation, plus a confidence line.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-paper">
    <div class="container grid-split">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="overline">The firewall</p>
        <h2>What it does. What it does not.</h2>
        <p class="measure mt-4">
          The Decision does arithmetic on numbers you give it, tagged as derived, so a claim like "roughly 8% of
          revenue" is shown as worked, not asserted. It does not build a financial model, a valuation, a template,
          a board pack or a risk register. That deeper modelling work is a separate product, The Case. The
          Decision's job is the call and the brief, not the spreadsheet behind it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="card">
          <ul class="marked">
            <li><span>Does:</span> arithmetic on given numbers, tagged given or derived</li>
            <li><span>Does:</span> a five-part, evidence-tagged brief in markdown</li>
            <li><span>Does not:</span> build a financial model or valuation</li>
            <li><span>Does not:</span> produce a deck, a template, or a risk register</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="card hygiene-box reveal">
        <p class="overline">Enterprise-paste hygiene</p>
        <h3>Plain markdown. Runs in your own account. Nothing collected.</h3>
        <p class="small mt-3 maxw-60ch">
          The Decision is a plain markdown file: no links, no embedded code, no macros, nothing that phones home.
          It runs entirely inside the AI account you already use. GreenSquare does not see your decision, your
          answers, or your brief. You can paste it into a work account under the same policies you already apply
          to any text you type into that account.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-dark" id="pricing">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="overline">Pricing</p>
      <div class="pricing-grid">
        <div class="price-card">
          <p class="mono price-tag">Individual</p>
          <h2>The Decision</h2>
          <p class="mt-4"><span class="price-now">$49</span> <span class="price-was">$59</span></p>
          <ul class="marked mt-6">
            <li>One file, yours to keep, no subscription</li>
            <li>Works in Claude and GPT</li>
            <li>Twelve months of model-version updates included</li>
            <li>Refund on request within 14 days</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn btn-on-dark mt-8" href="https://buy.stripe.com/aFaaEWfGDc7W7XF2wv3AY00" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get the Decision</a>
        </div>
        <div class="price-card">
          <p class="mono price-tag">Team, 10 seats</p>
          <h2>Team tier</h2>
          <p class="mt-4"><span class="price-now">A$490</span></p>
          <ul class="marked mt-6">
            <li>10 seats to the ladder</li>
            <li>One transaction, one relationship</li>
            <li>A quarterly briefing on how the benchmark has moved</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="text-action inline-block mt-8" href="mailto:hello@greensquare.ai?subject=Team%20tier">Write to hello@greensquare.ai</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="small mt-8 maxw-62ch">
        Priced below your expense-approval threshold on purpose. The maintenance moat is what protects it: your
        $49 includes 12 months of model-version updates and a re-run of the public benchmark within 14 days of
        each major frontier model release, so the file keeps being tested against the model you are actually
        running it on.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="overline">Questions</p>
      <h2>The short answers.</h2>
      <div class="faq-list mt-8">
        <details open>
          <summary>What exactly do I get?</summary>
          <p class="small">One markdown file for Claude or GPT. Open a new chat, paste or upload it, describe your decision, answer its questions, and it produces a five-part Decision Brief in the conversation.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need to install anything?</summary>
          <p class="small">No. It is a plain text file. No app, no plugin, no account with GreenSquare.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is it a subscription?</summary>
          <p class="small">No. One file, one price: $49, anchored to $59, with 12 months of model-version updates included.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Will it build me a financial model?</summary>
          <p class="small">No. It does arithmetic on numbers you give it, tagged as derived. Financial modelling is a separate product, The Case.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is it just a prompt someone could copy?</summary>
          <p class="small">It is a file, and that is the point: nothing to install, your data never leaves your own account. What is harder to copy is the standing commitment behind it: a published rubric, readable transcripts, and a benchmark re-run within 14 days of every major model release. See the <a href="/benchmark/">benchmark</a> and <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* hero specimen is the page's elevated object */
  .specimen-card { box-shadow: var(--shadow-specimen-dark); }
  .specimen-tag { color: var(--lime); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .specimen-list-simple { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--sp-4); color: var(--cream); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--size-stat-sub); }
  .stage-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: var(--sp-6); margin-top: var(--sp-12); }
  @media (max-width: 1040px) { .stage-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .stage-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .stage-num { color: var(--accent); font-size: 1rem; }
  .output-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: var(--sp-6); margin-top: var(--sp-12); }
  .output-grid .card span { color: var(--accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .output-grid .card h3 { margin-top: var(--sp-2); }
  @media (max-width: 1040px) { .output-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .output-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .hygiene-box { background: var(--bg); border-style: dashed; }
  .pricing-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--sp-8); margin-top: var(--sp-8); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .pricing-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .price-card { border: 1px solid var(--cream-18); border-radius: var(--radius-card); padding: var(--sp-8); }
  .price-tag { color: var(--lime); }
  .price-now { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--size-stat); color: var(--cream); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .price-was { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--size-stat-sub); color: var(--cream-60); text-decoration: line-through; margin-left: var(--sp-2); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .price-card .marked li { color: var(--cream); }
  .price-card .marked li::before { background: var(--lime); }
  .faq-list details { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-block: var(--sp-4); }
  .faq-list summary { font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; font-size: var(--size-h4); }
  .faq-list p { margin-top: var(--sp-3); }
</style>
